"Service","name":"Roof & Hail Claim Appraisal","serviceType":"Insurance appraisal","description":"Roof hail claim appraisal in Maine for asphalt, cedar, slate and standing-seam metal roofs when the carrier pays for repairs instead of a roof.","provider":{"@id":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"areaServed":{"@type":"State","name":"Maine"},"url":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-work/roof-hail-loss-appraisal/","image":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/shingles.webp","@id":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-work/roof-hail-loss-appraisal/#service"},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Maine get enough hail for a roof claim?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Hail is less frequent than in some regions, but summer storms do damage roofs in western and interior Maine. A dated storm report and photos of soft metal damage help show it happened."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a roof hail claim appraisal in Maine require a full replacement?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Appraisal sets the amount of loss, and in many files that amount reflects the cost to replace a roof that cannot be repaired or matched. Coverage limits in your policy still apply."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What about slate and cedar roofs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Both need specialized labor and materials. We price them as they are, not as asphalt shingles, which is a common source of underpayment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"My policy has a separate wind and hail deductible. Does that change appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The deductible is applied after the amount of loss is set. A percentage deductible can be large, so check the dollar figure before deciding whether appraisal is worth it."}}],"@id":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-work/roof-hail-loss-appraisal/#faq"}]}</script>
